## 2. Core Products / Services Landscape

Although this file’s emphasis is on history, understanding LEGO’s product and service lines clarifies how the company evolved.  From a single line of wooden pull‑toys, LEGO now offers a diversified ecosystem of physical toys, digital experiences and branded attractions.  Key categories include:

- **LEGO System Sets** – The core product line comprises interlocking brick sets across themes such as **City**, **Star Wars**, **NINJAGO**, **Technic**, **Friends**, **Harry Potter** and numerous others.  These sets adhere to the stud‑and‑tube standard patented in 1958【344533715736306†L16-L26】.
- **DUPLO** – Launched in 1969, DUPLO bricks are twice the size of standard bricks and designed for preschool children【682976293639197†L35-L41】.  DUPLO products emphasise everyday scenarios and role‑play to support early learning.
- **Technic** – Introduced in the late 1970s, Technic sets enable advanced mechanical constructions using gears, axles and pneumatics.  They cater to older children and adults, fostering engineering literacy.  *(Note: LEGO does not provide an official history article for Technic; the year 1977 is widely reported.)*
- **Mindstorms / Robotics & Coding** – Beginning with the MINDSTORMS Robotics Invention System in 1998, LEGO’s robotics kits combine programmable bricks with sensors and motors.  LEGO Education products incorporate MINDSTORMS and newer platforms (e.g., SPIKE Prime) to teach STEM skills【650828966092506†L93-L115】.
- **LEGO Education** – The Institutional Department established in 1980 provides curricula, teacher guides and hands‑on learning kits for schools【650828966092506†L9-L16】.
- **Licenced & Collaborative Themes** – Starting with **Star Wars** (1999), LEGO has partnered with IP owners—e.g., Disney (Marvel, Frozen), Warner Bros., NASA—to produce co‑branded sets.  These alliances will be explored further in Section 7.
- **Experiences & Attractions** – **LEGOLAND** parks (owned and operated by Merlin Entertainments under licence since 2005)【316149714439182†L70-L79】, **LEGO House** in Billund, and brand stores provide immersive experiences.
- **Digital & Games** – LEGO has produced video games (e.g., LEGO Island, LEGO Fortnite), mobile apps and digital building platforms.  Digital integration continues to evolve under current leadership.

